1
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,163
JIM: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:07,138
On the count of three, instead of telling
me who you love, tell me who to kill.

3
00:00:07,307 --> 00:00:10,004
- Kill Lee.
- You chose Lee because you love Vale.

4
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:11,410
(GRUNTS)

5
00:00:11,645 --> 00:00:14,638
ALICE: <i>If a person comes into
contact with my blood, it changes them.</i>

6
00:00:17,351 --> 00:00:19,820
Listen to me, I would never
do anything to hurt you.

7
00:00:20,521 --> 00:00:22,080
Kristen? No!

8
00:00:22,322 --> 00:00:25,258
You wanted to save Lee. You
knew he would do the opposite.

9
00:00:25,425 --> 00:00:27,257
You love Lee. Which
means we're done.

10
00:00:27,427 --> 00:00:29,293
I have found someone.
I have no choice

11
00:00:29,496 --> 00:00:31,488
- but to confess my feelings to Ed.
<i>- Da.</i>

12
00:00:31,665 --> 00:00:34,110
Is this is about the tests they're
running on Alice Tetch's blood?

13
00:00:34,134 --> 00:00:37,400
LUCIUS: <i>Yes. The rats were
exhibiting manic tendencies. Violent rage.</i>

14
00:00:37,638 --> 00:00:40,904
- I assume they're, uh, working on a cure.
- Yes, but it could take years.

15
00:00:41,074 --> 00:00:42,406
Nobody move!

16
00:00:42,576 --> 00:00:43,635
What is going on?

17
00:00:43,810 --> 00:00:45,490
I'm afraid your evening
has been hijacked.

18
00:00:45,612 --> 00:00:47,080
BULLOCK: Glasses down!

19
00:00:47,514 --> 00:00:48,641
(GRUNTING)

20
00:00:48,815 --> 00:00:52,343
Is that my dear sister I
see? She's in you, isn't she?

21
00:00:52,519 --> 00:00:54,215
- Ms. Kringle?
- No, my name's Isabella.

22
00:00:54,388 --> 00:00:56,148
You remind me of
someone that I used to know.

23
00:00:56,256 --> 00:00:58,384
I met someone. I think
I'm in love! (LAUGHS)

24
00:00:58,592 --> 00:01:00,117
I want to rejoin the GCPD.

25
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:02,457
Welcome back, Detective.

26
00:02:07,861 --> 00:02:09,523
(LIQUID SLOSHING)

27
00:02:16,603 --> 00:02:19,437
GCPD! Hands in the air!

28
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:20,903
Back away slowly.

29
00:02:22,542 --> 00:02:23,542
(SIGHS)

30
00:02:23,744 --> 00:02:27,044
- This ain't what it looks like.
- Explain it to me down at the precinct.

31
00:02:27,214 --> 00:02:29,843
For now, you'd be wise
to keep your mouth shut...

32
00:02:36,657 --> 00:02:38,717
Listen, uh, can
we talk about this?

33
00:02:39,893 --> 00:02:41,657
<i>Uh, be reasonable, man.</i>

34
00:02:42,562 --> 00:02:45,054
- (GROANING)
- Look, I didn't kill anybody, okay?

35
00:02:45,432 --> 00:02:47,560
I'm the cleaner. That's it.

36
00:02:48,435 --> 00:02:50,802
- You're just the cleaner.
- Yeah.

37
00:02:52,873 --> 00:02:56,275
Just the guy who chops up the
bodies and dumps them in a vat of acid.

38
00:02:56,476 --> 00:02:57,476
That's it.

39
00:03:01,915 --> 00:03:03,907
<i>What're you doing, man?</i>

40
00:03:04,317 --> 00:03:07,287
(SHUDDERS) Okay?
Just take me in, okay?

41
00:03:07,487 --> 00:03:10,946
Oh, I bet that's what you want.
For me to read you your rights.

42
00:03:11,425 --> 00:03:12,505
Make sure you get a lawyer.

43
00:03:12,592 --> 00:03:16,222
Two, three years from now, I see
you on some corner, free as a bird.

44
00:03:16,396 --> 00:03:20,163
Any other night, yeah.
It would eat at me,

45
00:03:21,168 --> 00:03:22,898
but, yeah, I'd do it.

46
00:03:23,804 --> 00:03:24,965
Not tonight.

47
00:03:25,138 --> 00:03:26,333
(BREATH TREMBLING)

48
00:03:26,506 --> 00:03:29,806
The Toad, he's the one you
want. He gave me the job.

49
00:03:29,976 --> 00:03:32,070
See, something's gotten into me.

50
00:03:32,646 --> 00:03:36,139
When I see a scumbag like you
my blood starts boiling in my veins.

51
00:03:36,316 --> 00:03:39,411
I just wanna punish
you, make you suffer.

52
00:03:39,853 --> 00:03:42,948
Up until now, I've
been able to control it.

53
00:03:44,658 --> 00:03:47,184
But it's getting
stronger inside of me.

54
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:48,760
Please,

55
00:03:48,929 --> 00:03:53,424
The Toad, I told you. He's
the one. Just arrest me.

56
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:54,761
Arrest me!

57
00:03:54,935 --> 00:03:57,131
- We're past that. (SCREAMS)
- Please! (SCREAMS)

58
00:03:57,304 --> 00:03:59,296
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

59
00:04:04,678 --> 00:04:07,079
- Morning.
- We knew what we were getting into, right?

60
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:10,581
When we agreed to let my dad
throw us an engagement party?

61
00:04:10,784 --> 00:04:13,015
(LAUGHING) Oh, we knew.

62
00:04:13,186 --> 00:04:14,950
I mean, who are these
people? (CHUCKLES)

63
00:04:15,222 --> 00:04:18,158
He's very proud of you. And he
wants all of Gotham to know that.

64
00:04:18,391 --> 00:04:21,088
Well, he's succeeded, because
he invited most of the city.

65
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:22,320
(BOTH CHUCKLING)

66
00:04:22,696 --> 00:04:25,860
- How are you so okay with this?
- Because I agree with him.

67
00:04:26,133 --> 00:04:28,261
He should be proud. As am I.

68
00:04:30,470 --> 00:04:31,733
How did I get so lucky?

69
00:04:39,079 --> 00:04:40,274
What is it?

70
00:04:44,151 --> 00:04:47,053
James Gordon is
returning to the GCPD.

71
00:04:48,021 --> 00:04:50,513
- When?
- He starts today.

72
00:04:52,759 --> 00:04:56,457
- Um, how long have you known this?
- A few days.

73
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:59,327
I'm sorry, I should've
told you sooner.

74
00:05:00,233 --> 00:05:01,565
It's fine.

75
00:05:02,769 --> 00:05:03,930
Is it?

76
00:05:04,704 --> 00:05:06,138
I don't know, Lee.

77
00:05:07,174 --> 00:05:09,336
We agreed he wouldn't
be part of our lives,

78
00:05:09,543 --> 00:05:12,221
and now you're gonna be working
with him. That's a part of our lives.

79
00:05:12,245 --> 00:05:16,740
Do you trust me? Because if
you do, then nothing else matters.

80
00:05:19,119 --> 00:05:20,883
Of course I trust you.

81
00:05:21,288 --> 00:05:24,850
And you're right, you're right.
It's all gonna be okay. It's just...

82
00:05:25,025 --> 00:05:26,769
(SIGHS) When I think about
what happened with Tetch

83
00:05:26,793 --> 00:05:29,209
and, and the things
that Gordon said, I...

84
00:05:29,233 --> 00:05:30,730
So, don't think about it.

85
00:05:32,032 --> 00:05:33,091
I'll try.

86
00:05:34,601 --> 00:05:38,663
But if you accidentally shot
him, I'd be okay with that, too.

87
00:05:38,839 --> 00:05:40,273
(CHUCKLES) No promises.

88
00:05:42,042 --> 00:05:43,840
I'll see you tonight.

89
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:46,438
Yeah.

90
00:05:54,254 --> 00:05:56,621
OFFICER 1: Lock this bum up.
OFFICER 2: Get out! Come on.

91
00:05:57,123 --> 00:05:58,751
MAN: I'm innocent, I tell ya!

92
00:05:59,226 --> 00:06:00,524
OFFICER 3: <i>Cover the alley.</i>

93
00:06:00,861 --> 00:06:03,456
- Look, stop pulling me so much.
- Hey, you're cute.

94
00:06:03,663 --> 00:06:05,154
Hey, hey, hey!

95
00:06:05,332 --> 00:06:08,359
There you are. We got a call,
Warehouse district. You coming?

96
00:06:08,568 --> 00:06:10,161
That's it? No welcome back?

97
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:13,363
Please. If we had a big to-do every
time you came back to the GCPD,

98
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:16,476
we'd never catch any
bad guys. <i>Ándale,</i> partner.

99
00:06:16,643 --> 00:06:20,546
Oh, and, uh... I believe,
this belongs to you.

100
00:06:23,783 --> 00:06:25,411
You coming or what?

101
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:27,782
Yeah. I'm coming.

102
00:06:30,724 --> 00:06:33,353
What must be broken
before it can be used?

103
00:06:33,526 --> 00:06:35,586
- (CHUCKLES) Eggs!
- Correct.

104
00:06:35,862 --> 00:06:38,024
- As always.
- (GASPS)

105
00:06:39,466 --> 00:06:42,095
Mmm, Edward, you spoil me.

106
00:06:42,669 --> 00:06:44,228
You make it easy.

107
00:06:46,406 --> 00:06:48,272
I'm going to miss you.

108
00:06:48,508 --> 00:06:50,409
I'm only gone two days.

109
00:06:50,644 --> 00:06:54,308
Well, actually, your conference
ends at 1:45 on Monday.

110
00:06:55,148 --> 00:06:58,312
With traffic, that puts
you in at 5:30 into Gotham.

111
00:06:58,551 --> 00:07:01,521
If you leave on time today,
which I'm sure that you will.

112
00:07:01,688 --> 00:07:04,157
- Mmm-hmm.
- You'll be gone 44 and one half hours.

113
00:07:05,692 --> 00:07:06,853
Less than two days.

114
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:08,389
(CHUCKLES)

115
00:07:08,728 --> 00:07:10,560
I will hold onto that thought.

116
00:07:10,730 --> 00:07:12,665
Cream! I forgot your cream.

117
00:07:13,199 --> 00:07:14,199
Mmm, mmm, mmm!

118
00:07:14,367 --> 00:07:18,236
So what does one do at
a librarians' conference?

119
00:07:19,072 --> 00:07:20,836
It would bore you.

120
00:07:21,541 --> 00:07:25,410
Nothing that you would say,
do, or think could bore me.

121
00:07:26,179 --> 00:07:29,445
Oh. In that case, let me
read you my schedule.

122
00:07:29,616 --> 00:07:30,777
- ED: Whoo!
- (CHUCKLES)

123
00:07:32,752 --> 00:07:34,118
(WHISTLES)

124
00:07:34,421 --> 00:07:35,514
(CLEARS THROAT)

125
00:07:37,824 --> 00:07:39,622
Where did those
glasses come from?

126
00:07:39,793 --> 00:07:43,457
These? These are my back-up
pair. I normally wear contacts.

127
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:45,155
(GASPS) I thought you knew that.

128
00:07:45,365 --> 00:07:46,492
(GULPS)

129
00:07:46,933 --> 00:07:48,128
Is something wrong?

130
00:07:52,005 --> 00:07:53,769
Edward, what is it?

131
00:07:54,374 --> 00:07:56,343
You look like
you've seen a ghost.

132
00:07:57,811 --> 00:07:59,177
Excuse me.

133
00:08:01,514 --> 00:08:03,574
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

134
00:08:12,092 --> 00:08:13,458
It's just a pair of glasses.

135
00:08:14,094 --> 00:08:15,756
(CONTINUES BREATHING HEAVILY)

136
00:08:16,429 --> 00:08:18,830
KRINGLE: <i>I remember
you loved that style on me.</i>

137
00:08:19,132 --> 00:08:20,132
(GASPS)

138
00:08:23,837 --> 00:08:25,430
(GASPS) Oh, dear.

139
00:08:26,906 --> 00:08:29,967
I haven't upset you,
have I, Ed? (GIGGLES)

140
00:08:30,243 --> 00:08:34,078
I would've thought you would've
been used to seeing people in mirrors.

141
00:08:34,414 --> 00:08:35,609
You're just in my head.

142
00:08:36,116 --> 00:08:37,709
Like that makes a difference.

143
00:08:37,917 --> 00:08:41,319
But honestly, besides the
fact that she looks just like me,

144
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:45,356
you went from someone who
files papers in a police station

145
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:49,394
to someone who files books in
a library. That's super original.

146
00:08:49,629 --> 00:08:51,530
You and Isabella are...

147
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:55,228
You're somewhat different.

148
00:08:55,402 --> 00:08:57,303
Well, I'm dead.

149
00:08:57,470 --> 00:08:59,200
(CHUCKLES) And she's alive.

150
00:09:00,407 --> 00:09:01,807
<i>But how long will that last?</i>

151
00:09:03,610 --> 00:09:05,738
- Until you...
- I...

152
00:09:06,312 --> 00:09:07,837
(MIMICS CHOKING)

153
00:09:08,515 --> 00:09:11,041
I would never hurt Isabella.

154
00:09:11,251 --> 00:09:14,380
Bet you would've said
the same thing about me.

155
00:09:15,755 --> 00:09:18,418
Face it, Ed. You're a killer.

156
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:21,528
It's only matter of time...

157
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:25,493
(SIGHING)

158
00:09:31,404 --> 00:09:32,997
BULLOCK: Okay, so.

159
00:09:33,239 --> 00:09:34,832
A Uni ID'd the vic.

160
00:09:35,008 --> 00:09:37,910
One Paulie Penopolus,
aka Paulie Pennies.

161
00:09:38,078 --> 00:09:39,989
- Clean up guy for the Gotham underworld.
- Bingo.

162
00:09:40,013 --> 00:09:43,381
I'm thinking it was some kind of business
deal. Maybe an unhappy customer.

163
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:44,846
Perhaps a competitor?

164
00:09:45,051 --> 00:09:48,453
Good place to start.
Hey, listen, seriously, Jim,

165
00:09:49,255 --> 00:09:50,450
I'm glad you're back.

166
00:09:51,091 --> 00:09:53,185
Me too, Harv. Feels good.

167
00:09:55,795 --> 00:09:57,661
(CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING)

168
00:10:07,006 --> 00:10:08,531
(OFFICER GAGGING)

169
00:10:11,344 --> 00:10:13,836
This wasn't just business.

170
00:10:14,447 --> 00:10:16,348
We should call Barnes.

171
00:10:25,225 --> 00:10:27,160
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

172
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:30,286
Do you know why I'm here?

173
00:10:32,699 --> 00:10:36,192
Oh, yes. Yes, indeed.

174
00:10:36,870 --> 00:10:38,930
She's in there, isn't she?

175
00:10:39,672 --> 00:10:41,197
Inside of you.

176
00:10:45,612 --> 00:10:47,376
Hello, sister dear.

177
00:10:54,587 --> 00:10:56,078
Just tell me,

178
00:10:57,190 --> 00:11:00,957
you grew up with your sister,
you've seen this virus first hand.

179
00:11:01,161 --> 00:11:02,789
How do I beat it?

180
00:11:03,496 --> 00:11:08,491
Hmm, I believe the
way this works is

181
00:11:08,668 --> 00:11:13,436
you give me something. I
give you something. Tick-tock.

182
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:16,235
- How's about I let you keep your teeth?
- Or?

183
00:11:17,277 --> 00:11:19,303
My sister's virus
is a beautiful thing,

184
00:11:19,479 --> 00:11:22,039
it makes the darkest
parts of a person sing.

185
00:11:23,650 --> 00:11:26,051
What darkness in you

186
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:29,446
has Alice brought to life?

187
00:11:30,823 --> 00:11:33,952
Tell me that, and I'll tell
you everything I know.

188
00:11:42,068 --> 00:11:43,127
Criminals.

189
00:11:44,737 --> 00:11:46,103
The guilty.

190
00:11:47,707 --> 00:11:49,005
My anger at them.

191
00:11:50,009 --> 00:11:52,979
Oh, but it's not anger I see.

192
00:11:54,514 --> 00:11:55,812
Rage.

193
00:11:57,183 --> 00:12:00,950
Violent, bloody rage.

194
00:12:03,990 --> 00:12:06,186
All right, Tetch, my turn.

195
00:12:06,426 --> 00:12:08,122
Is there a cure?

196
00:12:08,428 --> 00:12:09,623
(SIGHS)

197
00:12:12,532 --> 00:12:15,696
Yes, there is a cure.

198
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:18,231
What is it?

199
00:12:20,607 --> 00:12:23,839
You give in, and let my
dear sister win. (LAUGHS)

200
00:12:24,477 --> 00:12:25,740
You think I'm playing!

201
00:12:26,045 --> 00:12:29,106
- Have you heard the voices?
- What voices?

202
00:12:29,382 --> 00:12:32,079
The virus, even as it grows
stronger, waxes and wanes.

203
00:12:32,252 --> 00:12:35,689
You may have the
illusion you're winning.

204
00:12:36,923 --> 00:12:38,289
Then you hear the voices,

205
00:12:39,892 --> 00:12:43,693
those dark voices
from deep within you,

206
00:12:44,197 --> 00:12:47,429
whispering, whispering.

207
00:12:48,735 --> 00:12:53,173
And, finally, you'll see
the world as it really is.

208
00:12:53,406 --> 00:12:57,207
Then there will be no
more Captain Barnes.

209
00:12:57,977 --> 00:12:59,275
Only Alice.

210
00:13:00,613 --> 00:13:01,706
My dear Alice.

211
00:13:01,914 --> 00:13:03,041
(GRUNTS)

212
00:13:03,349 --> 00:13:04,544
You don't know me!

213
00:13:04,717 --> 00:13:06,777
You've dirtied your
hands, haven't you?

214
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:10,821
And now you're desperately
trying to make it right.

215
00:13:13,726 --> 00:13:15,194
I can make it right.

216
00:13:19,699 --> 00:13:21,497
- (KNOCKS ON DOOR)
- (DOOR BUZZES)

217
00:13:29,742 --> 00:13:30,801
You're back.

218
00:13:32,478 --> 00:13:33,741
I'm back.

219
00:13:35,148 --> 00:13:36,810
I suppose it was
only a matter of time.

220
00:13:37,717 --> 00:13:39,709
Once a cop, always a cop.

221
00:13:48,561 --> 00:13:51,463
For better or worse,
this is where I belong.

222
00:13:52,732 --> 00:13:54,928
- How's Vale?
- Good. I think.

223
00:13:55,601 --> 00:13:57,161
Well, she's out of
the hospital anyway.

224
00:13:57,904 --> 00:13:59,634
- You two are not...
- No.

225
00:14:02,809 --> 00:14:04,710
I'm not trying to
make this awkward.

226
00:14:04,944 --> 00:14:07,413
Why would it be?
We're both adults.

227
00:14:07,613 --> 00:14:10,138
There's no reason
we can't work together.

228
00:14:10,162 --> 00:14:12,711
I'm glad you feel that
way. Mario agrees?

229
00:14:12,885 --> 00:14:15,787
- He will. Eventually.
- Right.

230
00:14:17,056 --> 00:14:18,388
Our engagement party is tonight.

231
00:14:19,025 --> 00:14:21,893
I only bring it up because a
few people here are going.

232
00:14:23,162 --> 00:14:25,131
- Now it's awkward, isn't it?
- A little.

233
00:14:26,599 --> 00:14:27,976
You wanna know
about the two bodies

234
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,559
- that, were found this morning?
- Yes.

235
00:14:29,736 --> 00:14:31,416
I've only done the
preliminary examination.

236
00:14:31,504 --> 00:14:35,464
But that John Doe in the acid?
His face had been removed.

237
00:14:35,641 --> 00:14:36,768
Removed? How?

238
00:14:36,976 --> 00:14:40,242
Scalpel? Razor blade? Whoever did
it knew exactly what they were doing.

239
00:14:40,413 --> 00:14:43,042
- I'll have more for you soon.
- Okay.

240
00:14:43,249 --> 00:14:44,945
Jim.

241
00:14:46,052 --> 00:14:48,180
I think you made the right
decision, coming back.

242
00:15:01,167 --> 00:15:03,946
BULLOCK: (DISTORTED) I know this
doesn't exactly look like just business.

243
00:15:03,970 --> 00:15:05,114
But, right now, we're thinking

244
00:15:05,138 --> 00:15:07,216
(CLEARLY) whoever paid Paulie
Pennies to dispose of the body

245
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:11,405
in the bathtub also might have
killed him to tie up some loose ends.

246
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:12,601
<i>Uh-huh.</i>

247
00:15:14,881 --> 00:15:18,716
Jim, good to see you with
a shield again. And a tie.

248
00:15:18,885 --> 00:15:21,821
- Captain. Good to be back.
- Bullock was just filling me in.

249
00:15:21,988 --> 00:15:24,822
- Hell of a one to catch on your first day.
- Yeah. (SIGHS)

250
00:15:24,991 --> 00:15:27,085
It's the preliminary
report from Lee.

251
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:29,957
John Doe had his face removed.

252
00:15:31,197 --> 00:15:32,722
Trying to cover up his identity?

253
00:15:32,899 --> 00:15:36,165
I don't know, maybe. But the
acid would've done that anyway.

254
00:15:36,335 --> 00:15:37,633
I'm running point on this one.

255
00:15:37,804 --> 00:15:39,796
- Honestly, Captain...
- That's cool.

256
00:15:42,275 --> 00:15:43,635
Uh, look, I know
I've been away...

257
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:46,871
Maybe that's why you've
forgotten how things go around here.

258
00:15:47,046 --> 00:15:50,346
- I give you an order, and you follow it.
- Which, for the record, Captain,

259
00:15:50,516 --> 00:15:51,711
I totally support.

260
00:15:51,884 --> 00:15:54,353
I'm taking point on this. I'm
not giving you the day off.

261
00:15:54,687 --> 00:15:56,553
<i>Follow the physical
evidence, Bullock.</i>

262
00:15:57,056 --> 00:15:59,116
- Report back to me.
- Aye aye.

263
00:16:00,393 --> 00:16:01,656
Jim,

264
00:16:05,865 --> 00:16:08,164
I didn't mean to
bite your head off.

265
00:16:08,334 --> 00:16:11,429
It's just sometimes the
ugliness here gets to me.

266
00:16:11,737 --> 00:16:13,933
No need to explain. Let me
know if you need anything.

267
00:16:14,540 --> 00:16:15,872
And, uh...

268
00:16:16,943 --> 00:16:20,107
Don't let the bastards
haze you too hard, rookie.

269
00:16:20,346 --> 00:16:22,315
(CHUCKLES) Yes, sir.

270
00:16:23,583 --> 00:16:24,778
Gordon.

271
00:16:25,685 --> 00:16:29,588
Here's the one you wanted, Captain.
Uh, mid-level felon. Goes by The Toad.

272
00:16:30,122 --> 00:16:32,421
Yeah, that's him. Thank you.

273
00:16:48,474 --> 00:16:50,102
ED: <i>Maybe she's right.</i>

274
00:16:50,343 --> 00:16:53,404
What if there's something
about Miss Kringle's... Kristen's...

275
00:16:53,646 --> 00:16:55,308
Isabella's face.

276
00:16:55,748 --> 00:16:59,014
What if there's something about
her face that unlocks this side of me?

277
00:16:59,852 --> 00:17:01,286
What if I do hurt her?

278
00:17:03,422 --> 00:17:05,982
- Oswald?
- Yes?

279
00:17:06,225 --> 00:17:07,488
You're smiling.

280
00:17:08,494 --> 00:17:09,894
- I was?
<i>- Yes.</i>

281
00:17:10,129 --> 00:17:11,961
Oh. (STAMMERS)

282
00:17:12,832 --> 00:17:14,562
I was just thinking

283
00:17:15,935 --> 00:17:18,928
how darned lucky Isabella is.

284
00:17:19,805 --> 00:17:24,072
You love her, yet to protect her
you are willing to break up with her.

285
00:17:25,511 --> 00:17:27,707
Beautiful. Sad.

286
00:17:27,914 --> 00:17:30,884
- But beautiful.
- So you think I should break up with her.

287
00:17:31,083 --> 00:17:33,985
Oh, I'm sorry. I thought that's
what we were talking about.

288
00:17:34,186 --> 00:17:37,645
- Oh. Certainly, I would never pressure...
- No, you're right.

289
00:17:41,327 --> 00:17:43,455
If I did hurt her, I would
never forgive myself.

290
00:17:44,397 --> 00:17:45,558
(SCOFFS)

291
00:17:46,032 --> 00:17:50,163
That life would put her in your path
again only to snatch her from you.

292
00:17:50,336 --> 00:17:51,998
- Why?
- I can't do it.

293
00:17:52,405 --> 00:17:54,840
- What?
- I can't break up with her.

294
00:17:55,875 --> 00:17:58,435
- But you said yourself...
- I need you to do it for me.

295
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:04,310
Would you do that? I
would be forever in your debt.

296
00:18:05,818 --> 00:18:07,286
Just be gentle.

297
00:18:10,790 --> 00:18:12,122
Of course.

298
00:18:25,671 --> 00:18:29,073
I'm looking for a punk who
supposedly frequents this rat hole.

299
00:18:29,408 --> 00:18:31,570
Goes by "The Toad."

300
00:18:32,612 --> 00:18:34,342
MAN: <i>Who's askin'?</i>

301
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:42,384
Captain Nathaniel
Barnes of the GCPD.

302
00:18:43,923 --> 00:18:45,334
How about you and I
go down to the precinct,

303
00:18:45,358 --> 00:18:47,589
and you can answer
some questions.

304
00:18:48,561 --> 00:18:49,893
Blow, pig.

305
00:18:50,062 --> 00:18:51,690
- (GRUNTING)
- (BONES CRUNCHING)

306
00:18:59,138 --> 00:19:00,299
(GROANING)

307
00:19:04,443 --> 00:19:05,570
(GLASS SHATTERS)

308
00:19:06,178 --> 00:19:08,079
I wanna know about
Paulie Pennies.

309
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:11,307
The body he was getting rid of
last night. Where did it come from?

310
00:19:11,484 --> 00:19:12,645
(BREATH TREMBLING)

311
00:19:13,052 --> 00:19:15,283
Maybe you want me to
open that mouth for you?

312
00:19:15,454 --> 00:19:18,686
Okay. Stop. I hired Paulie!

313
00:19:18,858 --> 00:19:20,827
- But I'm just the go-between!
- (GRUNTS)

314
00:19:20,993 --> 00:19:22,655
I'm getting so sick
of hearing that.

315
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:25,730
No one's responsible for
anything. Everyone's a middleman.

316
00:19:25,898 --> 00:19:28,629
- I want a name!
- Symon. Okay?

317
00:19:28,901 --> 00:19:32,633
And Dr. Symon. He's a
big time plastic surgeon!

318
00:19:33,005 --> 00:19:34,564
So, what?

319
00:19:34,740 --> 00:19:37,608
He likes cutting people's
faces off for kicks? Try again!

320
00:19:37,777 --> 00:19:39,905
No! He's got a side business.

321
00:19:40,112 --> 00:19:43,776
You get in trouble. You need
a new face. He gives you one!

322
00:19:44,817 --> 00:19:46,809
A new face? Whose?

323
00:19:47,086 --> 00:19:50,545
I don't know. I just get
rid of the bodies! That's all!

324
00:19:50,856 --> 00:19:52,085
(GROANING)

325
00:19:55,027 --> 00:19:59,397
Oh, you think you're
not guilty, but you are.

326
00:19:59,598 --> 00:20:02,659
Stop, okay? Stop! It's Symon.

327
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:05,303
(STUTTERS) <i>He's
the one you want!</i>

328
00:20:06,238 --> 00:20:07,866
You're a cop!

329
00:20:10,743 --> 00:20:12,109
(GASPING)

330
00:20:12,745 --> 00:20:14,509
Symon, huh?

331
00:20:15,114 --> 00:20:16,138
Take me to him.

332
00:20:22,088 --> 00:20:23,488
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

333
00:20:27,259 --> 00:20:28,557
Mayor Cobblepot?

334
00:20:28,761 --> 00:20:31,629
Hello, Isabella. May I?

335
00:20:32,364 --> 00:20:34,492
Um, of course.

336
00:20:40,005 --> 00:20:41,371
(COBBLEPOT SIGHS)

337
00:20:43,642 --> 00:20:45,133
Going somewhere?

338
00:20:45,311 --> 00:20:47,610
Just for a couple of nights.

339
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:50,306
But, I was hoping to
talk to Ed before I left.

340
00:20:50,516 --> 00:20:52,610
Um, tried calling
him. Is he okay?

341
00:20:53,486 --> 00:20:55,648
Hmm. Yes.

342
00:20:56,355 --> 00:20:57,448
How shall I put this?

343
00:21:00,226 --> 00:21:01,285
It's over. (CHUCKLES)

344
00:21:02,495 --> 00:21:03,929
Excuse me?

345
00:21:04,096 --> 00:21:07,726
He is not going to see you
anymore. Do not try to contact him.

346
00:21:07,967 --> 00:21:09,230
That door is closed.

347
00:21:10,736 --> 00:21:11,829
Have a nice life.

348
00:21:14,273 --> 00:21:15,639
Oh... (GASPS)

349
00:21:17,510 --> 00:21:19,103
Oh, my. (SNIFFS)

350
00:21:20,079 --> 00:21:21,445
It is a shock.

351
00:21:21,747 --> 00:21:26,185
But, besides your odd
resemblance to his ex,

352
00:21:27,553 --> 00:21:29,419
a certain facility with riddles,

353
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:33,088
compulsion for order,

354
00:21:33,859 --> 00:21:36,226
what is it that you two
really have in common?

355
00:21:36,896 --> 00:21:40,958
<i>Edward is a person of exceptional
intelligence and imagination.</i>

356
00:21:41,534 --> 00:21:44,231
He deserves to be appreciated
by someone on his own level.

357
00:21:44,904 --> 00:21:49,069
And you, my dear,
are simply not.

358
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:52,108
Best to end things now.

359
00:21:53,946 --> 00:21:55,380
You're right.

360
00:21:56,515 --> 00:21:57,744
I don't deserve him.

361
00:21:59,018 --> 00:22:01,249
Glad we agree. Bye.

362
00:22:01,487 --> 00:22:03,683
But I'm not gonna let him go.

363
00:22:04,723 --> 00:22:08,785
(SNIFFLES) He loves
me, and I love him.

364
00:22:09,428 --> 00:22:12,159
Do you know how
rare that is, Mr. Mayor?

365
00:22:12,464 --> 00:22:13,762
(INHALES SHARPLY)

366
00:22:18,037 --> 00:22:19,972
Of course, you do.

367
00:22:21,774 --> 00:22:23,208
Because you love him, too.

368
00:22:25,177 --> 00:22:26,941
I can see it.

369
00:22:27,179 --> 00:22:29,978
(SIGHS) I'm not even jealous.

370
00:22:30,983 --> 00:22:34,181
- I don't think that you understand...
- It was my glasses this morning.

371
00:22:34,353 --> 00:22:36,219
They reminded
him of Miss Kringle.

372
00:22:36,388 --> 00:22:39,381
He's afraid he's going to
hurt me like he hurt her.

373
00:22:43,062 --> 00:22:45,531
Listen to me, you little idiot,

374
00:22:46,232 --> 00:22:47,928
I am telling you one last time.

375
00:22:48,100 --> 00:22:50,365
Let Ed go.

376
00:22:50,569 --> 00:22:51,764
No.

377
00:22:52,504 --> 00:22:55,406
I will write to him. I will
make him understand

378
00:22:55,574 --> 00:22:58,806
he has nothing to fear.
I'm not gonna let him go.

379
00:22:59,044 --> 00:23:01,206
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

380
00:23:01,614 --> 00:23:03,845
(CHUCKLES) Very well.

381
00:23:04,750 --> 00:23:06,616
Don't say I didn't warn you.

382
00:23:12,057 --> 00:23:13,286
(SIGHS)

383
00:23:23,135 --> 00:23:25,570
- You better not have been lying to me.
- I'm not.

384
00:23:25,738 --> 00:23:29,140
This is his place. You're
not going to kill me, are you?

385
00:23:31,610 --> 00:23:32,805
I'm trying.

386
00:23:37,616 --> 00:23:39,656
- I'm about to take the face.
- (MUFFLED WHIMPERING)

387
00:23:39,818 --> 00:23:42,049
Be here in an hour, and
we can do the transplant.

388
00:23:42,955 --> 00:23:45,322
You haven't eaten
today, have you?

389
00:23:45,491 --> 00:23:47,119
Very good.

390
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:51,961
I have to thank you, my dear,
for taking such care of your skin.

391
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:54,862
Excellent elasticity.

392
00:23:55,801 --> 00:23:57,702
Now, hold still.

393
00:23:58,437 --> 00:24:00,030
(MUFFLED PROTESTING)

394
00:24:02,708 --> 00:24:04,233
(DOOR SLAMS OPEN)

395
00:24:05,744 --> 00:24:08,646
- Who's there? Quiet!
- (MUFFLED SHOUTING)

396
00:24:09,581 --> 00:24:11,709
Or we will forgo any anesthesia.

397
00:24:11,984 --> 00:24:14,954
- I said, who's there?
- GCPD.

398
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:17,146
You're under arrest. Go for it.

399
00:24:18,824 --> 00:24:19,917
Please.

400
00:24:21,327 --> 00:24:22,386
(WHIMPERING)

401
00:24:23,862 --> 00:24:27,299
- I surrender.
- Ma'am, you all right?

402
00:24:40,479 --> 00:24:41,503
(SNARLS SOFTLY)

403
00:24:41,714 --> 00:24:42,943
How many?

404
00:24:43,248 --> 00:24:45,240
- Excuse me?
- How many have you killed?

405
00:24:45,517 --> 00:24:47,713
How many faces have you taken?

406
00:24:49,121 --> 00:24:50,987
I have the right to an attorney.

407
00:24:51,690 --> 00:24:54,455
I wish to invoke
that right, now.

408
00:24:55,027 --> 00:24:58,429
VOICES: (WHISPERING)
<i>Guilty! Guilty! Guilty!</i>

409
00:24:58,630 --> 00:25:01,532
- Who's there?
- No one. It's only me.

410
00:25:03,435 --> 00:25:06,030
VOICES: <i>He's guilty.
Guilty. Guilty. Guilty. Guilty.</i>

411
00:25:06,338 --> 00:25:07,601
What is wrong with you?

412
00:25:08,874 --> 00:25:10,240
(GRUNTING)

413
00:25:13,078 --> 00:25:16,310
- (PANTS) What are you doing? Arrest me!
- (GUN COCKING)

414
00:25:16,482 --> 00:25:19,350
VOICES: <i>Guilty! Guilty!</i>

415
00:25:19,518 --> 00:25:20,645
I'm not resisting!

416
00:25:20,919 --> 00:25:21,943
<i>Guilty!</i>

417
00:25:22,354 --> 00:25:23,617
<i>Guilty!</i>

418
00:25:25,057 --> 00:25:26,150
<i>He's guilty!</i>

419
00:25:26,525 --> 00:25:27,788
<i>Guilty.</i>

420
00:25:31,563 --> 00:25:34,175
LUCIUS: <i>The point Dr. Thompkins
hopes you pay particular attention to</i>

421
00:25:34,199 --> 00:25:39,763
is the level of strength required to
sever Paulie Pennies' head from his torso.

422
00:25:40,439 --> 00:25:42,101
And what level
would that be, Lucius?

423
00:25:42,274 --> 00:25:43,274
Extreme.

424
00:25:43,475 --> 00:25:45,137
Extreme strength, got it.

425
00:25:45,310 --> 00:25:48,838
As for the other victim in the bathtub
we haven't gotten any hits on his prints.

426
00:25:49,081 --> 00:25:51,175
But a puncture mark
in his arm suggests

427
00:25:51,350 --> 00:25:53,819
he was drugged prior to
having his face removed.

428
00:25:54,119 --> 00:25:56,131
I'll run toxicology, let you
know what I come up with.

429
00:25:56,155 --> 00:25:57,987
- Thanks, Lucius.
- Yup.

430
00:25:59,024 --> 00:26:01,425
It's good to have
you back, Gordon.

431
00:26:01,627 --> 00:26:03,823
Lucius, you're in
forensics, not the ME.

432
00:26:04,029 --> 00:26:06,225
Is there a reason Lee
didn't bring this herself?

433
00:26:07,666 --> 00:26:11,535
Dr. Thompkins is already gone
for the day. Her engagement party.

434
00:26:13,672 --> 00:26:14,672
Right.

435
00:26:14,840 --> 00:26:17,071
I hear it's gonna
be quite the affair.

436
00:26:17,242 --> 00:26:20,041
Beautiful women.
Free booze. Canapés.

437
00:26:20,212 --> 00:26:22,010
Harvey, you can go if you want.

438
00:26:22,314 --> 00:26:26,012
I'd much rather spend time here
with my old partner. Much more fun.

439
00:26:26,819 --> 00:26:29,152
Besides, I wasn't invited.

440
00:26:29,321 --> 00:26:30,321
(CHUCKLES)

441
00:26:32,658 --> 00:26:33,658
Captain.

442
00:26:33,859 --> 00:26:37,694
Bullock, book this piece of human
garbage for the murder of John Doe.

443
00:26:37,863 --> 00:26:39,991
You got it, Captain. Come on.

444
00:26:41,333 --> 00:26:43,996
Plastic surgeon. Face
man for the underworld.

445
00:26:45,137 --> 00:26:47,197
He had a girl on the table.

446
00:26:47,372 --> 00:26:49,034
If I had been there
five minutes later...

447
00:26:49,208 --> 00:26:51,939
But you weren't.
You did it, Captain.

448
00:26:52,744 --> 00:26:54,975
Yeah, today.

449
00:26:58,016 --> 00:27:00,918
You know that feeling, Jim,
when you've won the battle

450
00:27:01,120 --> 00:27:02,782
but you know you're
gonna lose the war?

451
00:27:04,256 --> 00:27:06,691
Wars are fought one
battle at a time, sir.

452
00:27:10,295 --> 00:27:13,663
You said he killed the John
Doe. Not Paulie Pennies?

453
00:27:14,333 --> 00:27:16,564
No. His killer
is still out there.

454
00:27:17,736 --> 00:27:20,262
I'll get him
tomorrow. I promise.

455
00:28:03,282 --> 00:28:04,944
(PEOPLE CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

456
00:28:05,117 --> 00:28:06,117
MARIO: Ahem.

457
00:28:07,753 --> 00:28:11,520
My father and I haven't
always seen eye to eye.

458
00:28:11,690 --> 00:28:13,249
(ALL CHUCKLING)

459
00:28:13,959 --> 00:28:15,723
But I think, Dad,

460
00:28:15,894 --> 00:28:20,161
you'll agree that marrying Lee is
the best decision I've ever made.

461
00:28:20,966 --> 00:28:22,992
- Without a doubt.
- (ALL LAUGHING)

462
00:28:23,936 --> 00:28:26,496
And, Lee, you're a doctor,

463
00:28:26,905 --> 00:28:28,965
a member of our city's
police department,

464
00:28:30,442 --> 00:28:33,844
you're funny,
compassionate, and brilliant.

465
00:28:34,546 --> 00:28:39,314
Despite insisting all dogs
are boys and all cats are girls.

466
00:28:40,452 --> 00:28:43,081
It's hopeless, I've
tried to correct her.

467
00:28:44,656 --> 00:28:46,989
I have loved you since
the moment I saw you.

468
00:28:49,094 --> 00:28:51,086
- WOMAN: Aw!
- (ALL APPLAUD)

469
00:28:52,464 --> 00:28:53,932
(CHEERING)

470
00:28:56,201 --> 00:28:58,864
It's so wonderful. He's
sweet. You're so lucky.

471
00:28:59,071 --> 00:29:00,266
BARBARA: <i>Lee!</i>

472
00:29:01,506 --> 00:29:02,769
Congrats.

473
00:29:03,642 --> 00:29:05,372
You look gorgeous, no surprise.

474
00:29:05,544 --> 00:29:06,904
- Barbara? How did you...
- Get in?

475
00:29:07,212 --> 00:29:10,546
As a plus one. With
that guy there. Hey.

476
00:29:10,983 --> 00:29:12,023
Or it might have been him.

477
00:29:12,284 --> 00:29:13,877
You need to leave right now.

478
00:29:14,219 --> 00:29:16,711
Can't we bury the hatchet?
So I came at you with a knife,

479
00:29:16,888 --> 00:29:18,151
kidnapped you, whatever.

480
00:29:18,957 --> 00:29:21,677
I've forgiven you for beating me
unconscious. Water under the bridge.

481
00:29:21,860 --> 00:29:23,740
You just stay right here.
I'm gonna get someone.

482
00:29:23,829 --> 00:29:25,092
I'm leaving.

483
00:29:26,732 --> 00:29:28,064
I just wanted to ask.

484
00:29:28,267 --> 00:29:32,398
As someone else who was once
with Jim Gordon, don't you miss it?

485
00:29:32,638 --> 00:29:33,731
Miss what?

486
00:29:34,406 --> 00:29:35,669
The heat.

487
00:29:36,375 --> 00:29:40,210
Being so close, so
much darkness and light,

488
00:29:40,879 --> 00:29:43,348
to someone always
at war with himself.

489
00:29:43,615 --> 00:29:46,278
Let me think.
Tormented Jim Gordon.

490
00:29:46,451 --> 00:29:48,943
Or Mario, who I
know is a good man,

491
00:29:49,121 --> 00:29:51,317
who'll be a wonderful
father to my children,

492
00:29:51,556 --> 00:29:52,956
and whom I love.

493
00:29:53,558 --> 00:29:55,356
No, I don't miss it.

494
00:29:56,395 --> 00:29:57,454
Wow.

495
00:29:57,896 --> 00:29:59,558
I think you actually
believe that.

496
00:29:59,965 --> 00:30:01,729
(CHUCKLES) It's kind of sad.

497
00:30:02,934 --> 00:30:05,426
Tell my dates I've
left, would you?

498
00:30:07,406 --> 00:30:08,533
Uh-uh.

499
00:30:08,740 --> 00:30:10,470
- Don't let her ruin your night.
- (SIGHS)

500
00:30:10,676 --> 00:30:12,577
Captain, I'm so glad you came.

501
00:30:13,278 --> 00:30:16,305
I can't stay. I came
to congratulate you.

502
00:30:17,249 --> 00:30:18,683
You deserve to be happy.

503
00:30:19,518 --> 00:30:20,518
Thank you.

504
00:30:20,686 --> 00:30:22,406
But you have to stay
for at least one drink.

505
00:30:22,554 --> 00:30:25,524
If nothing else, to save
me from these people.

506
00:30:26,525 --> 00:30:27,584
One drink.

507
00:30:27,959 --> 00:30:29,928
- But no work talk.
- Deal.

508
00:30:31,997 --> 00:30:34,865
So, among the materials
confiscated in Symon's lab,

509
00:30:35,033 --> 00:30:37,696
I came across a unique
anesthetic cocktail.

510
00:30:37,869 --> 00:30:41,636
Let me guess, the same cocktail
toxicology found in the John Doe.

511
00:30:41,807 --> 00:30:42,807
Exactly.

512
00:30:43,842 --> 00:30:47,006
Hey. I got some bad
news. Symon walked.

513
00:30:47,245 --> 00:30:48,245
What?

514
00:30:48,513 --> 00:30:51,915
The girl he had tied up refused to
press charges, they probably paid her off,

515
00:30:52,117 --> 00:30:54,609
<i>and we just got an order
from Judge Bam-Bam</i>

516
00:30:54,820 --> 00:30:57,051
demanding his immediate release.

517
00:30:57,289 --> 00:31:00,225
The botoxed son of a
bitch is uber-connected.

518
00:31:00,392 --> 00:31:03,885
The toxicology definitely ties
Symon to the John Doe murder.

519
00:31:04,329 --> 00:31:06,264
We gotta get him back here.

520
00:31:10,969 --> 00:31:12,597
Captain Barnes?

521
00:31:14,473 --> 00:31:17,307
Carmine Falcone. I
don't believe we've met.

522
00:31:17,776 --> 00:31:20,610
No. But I was just leaving.

523
00:31:21,780 --> 00:31:24,579
I see. Is my company so odious?

524
00:31:25,117 --> 00:31:26,642
You belong behind bars.

525
00:31:27,586 --> 00:31:28,781
I'm retired.

526
00:31:28,987 --> 00:31:32,355
After running Gotham's
underworld for 30 years.

527
00:31:34,526 --> 00:31:36,961
This city was built
because of men like me.

528
00:31:37,262 --> 00:31:39,356
People have jobs
because of men like me.

529
00:31:39,531 --> 00:31:41,523
That whiskey you're drinking,

530
00:31:41,833 --> 00:31:43,131
paid for through my work.

531
00:31:43,335 --> 00:31:45,827
So you did some good. So what?

532
00:31:46,338 --> 00:31:48,136
<i>It doesn't mean
you're above the law.</i>

533
00:31:48,373 --> 00:31:49,568
Nobody is.

534
00:31:50,509 --> 00:31:54,002
You know, whenever I hear a
man possessed of such certainty,

535
00:31:54,279 --> 00:31:57,408
I always think he's trying
mostly to convince himself.

536
00:31:59,551 --> 00:32:02,248
I wish you a pleasant
evening, Captain.

537
00:32:10,562 --> 00:32:11,655
(SIGHS)

538
00:32:20,539 --> 00:32:21,539
(SIGHS)

539
00:32:21,740 --> 00:32:23,470
<i>- Hey, Cap.</i>
- Alvarez.

540
00:32:24,309 --> 00:32:28,940
Tell Gordon I'm bringing him the man
responsible for Paulie Pennies' murder.

541
00:32:29,214 --> 00:32:31,877
No backup. He's coming
in of his own accord.

542
00:32:32,250 --> 00:32:36,585
<i>Sure thing, Cap. But you should
know the judge released Dr. Symon.</i>

543
00:32:36,855 --> 00:32:38,653
<i>We had to let him go.</i>

544
00:32:39,858 --> 00:32:41,224
VOICES: (WHISPERING) <i>Guilty!</i>

545
00:32:41,560 --> 00:32:42,560
<i>Guilty!</i>

546
00:32:42,761 --> 00:32:44,229
<i>Guilty! Guilty!</i>

547
00:32:44,463 --> 00:32:46,056
<i>Guilty! Guilty!</i>

548
00:32:46,264 --> 00:32:47,459
<i>Guilty!</i>

549
00:32:47,632 --> 00:32:48,632
<i>Guilty!</i>

550
00:32:48,900 --> 00:32:50,562
<i>Guilty! Guilty!</i>

551
00:32:51,336 --> 00:32:52,668
Guilty.

552
00:33:00,846 --> 00:33:01,939
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

553
00:33:02,347 --> 00:33:03,610
Isabella?

554
00:33:08,887 --> 00:33:10,947
Isabella, I got your note.

555
00:33:12,924 --> 00:33:15,689
I thought you needed to
leave for your conference.

556
00:33:15,961 --> 00:33:17,486
ISABELLA: <i>I can be late, Edward.</i>

557
00:33:23,869 --> 00:33:25,633
This is more important.

558
00:33:28,573 --> 00:33:29,802
Oswald... (CLEARS THROAT)

559
00:33:32,310 --> 00:33:33,676
Oswald,

560
00:33:34,646 --> 00:33:37,047
the Mayor, he informed
me of your position.

561
00:33:37,249 --> 00:33:39,150
But believe me, I think

562
00:33:40,018 --> 00:33:41,486
our breaking up is for the best.

563
00:33:41,686 --> 00:33:44,485
<i>No, Edward, it's not.</i>

564
00:33:44,890 --> 00:33:48,827
<i>I understand your fear. It
comes from a place of love.</i>

565
00:33:49,594 --> 00:33:52,029
<i>I know you won't hurt me.</i>

566
00:33:54,199 --> 00:33:55,792
You never could.

567
00:33:56,368 --> 00:33:57,802
I don't think that you...

568
00:33:58,537 --> 00:33:59,596
(GASPS)

569
00:34:00,171 --> 00:34:01,469
Oh, my... (SHUDDERS)

570
00:34:03,108 --> 00:34:04,337
Kristen.

571
00:34:05,277 --> 00:34:07,610
I found old photos
in newspapers.

572
00:34:08,313 --> 00:34:10,509
- You have to...
- I need to leave. Now!

573
00:34:10,682 --> 00:34:13,151
No, no, no. Look at me!

574
00:34:13,552 --> 00:34:15,748
- Look at me!
- You don't know what you're doing.

575
00:34:15,921 --> 00:34:19,619
I am forcing you to face
your fear! You won't hurt me!

576
00:34:19,824 --> 00:34:22,316
Even when I look
like this! Edward!

577
00:34:22,961 --> 00:34:24,259
Edward.

578
00:34:26,698 --> 00:34:28,530
(BOTH BREATHING HEAVILY)

579
00:34:35,874 --> 00:34:38,343
No, no, no.

580
00:34:44,449 --> 00:34:45,712
Edward...

581
00:34:48,119 --> 00:34:49,119
(CHOKING) Edward.

582
00:34:58,463 --> 00:35:00,295
Should I take the glasses off?

583
00:35:00,532 --> 00:35:01,932
Keep 'em on.

584
00:35:11,109 --> 00:35:15,740
Seal off the exits. But do it quietly.
Last thing anyone wants is a scene.

585
00:35:15,914 --> 00:35:16,914
FEMALE OFFICER: <i>Yes, sir.</i>

586
00:35:17,082 --> 00:35:20,018
A little late for that.
What are you doing here?

587
00:35:20,285 --> 00:35:21,885
I'm sorry, but we
have to make an arrest

588
00:35:22,153 --> 00:35:24,622
in the Paulie Pennies case.
We tried to get the guy at home.

589
00:35:24,889 --> 00:35:26,100
But his housekeeper
said he was here.

590
00:35:26,124 --> 00:35:28,821
Just makes you realize what a
small town Gotham is, doesn't it?

591
00:35:28,994 --> 00:35:31,793
Couldn't you wait? If he's
here, he's not exactly running.

592
00:35:31,963 --> 00:35:34,228
She makes a good point,
Jim. You wanna take that one?

593
00:35:34,399 --> 00:35:35,731
Good evening, everyone.

594
00:35:36,901 --> 00:35:39,063
Jim, what's going on?

595
00:35:39,237 --> 00:35:42,071
Apparently, there's a murder
suspect among our guests.

596
00:35:42,240 --> 00:35:43,264
Can I ask who?

597
00:35:43,475 --> 00:35:45,171
Dr. Maxwell Symon. He's a...

598
00:35:45,377 --> 00:35:49,473
Plastic surgeon. You arrest him, you're
gonna have to fight off every woman here.

599
00:35:49,648 --> 00:35:50,648
He's a favorite.

600
00:35:50,882 --> 00:35:52,680
He's also a murderer.

601
00:35:53,885 --> 00:35:55,730
I'd be curious to know
how your father knows him.

602
00:35:55,754 --> 00:35:58,485
I'm sure that their relationship
is completely aboveboard.

603
00:35:58,690 --> 00:36:01,524
While you two hash this
out. I'm gonna go grab Symon.

604
00:36:01,693 --> 00:36:02,922
- Harvey.
- What?

605
00:36:03,094 --> 00:36:04,995
I can handle a plastic
surgeon on my own.

606
00:36:05,397 --> 00:36:08,231
Don't worry, discretion
is my middle name.

607
00:36:12,003 --> 00:36:13,562
Lee, I'd like a word with Jim.

608
00:36:13,738 --> 00:36:15,536
- Mario.
- It'll be fine.

609
00:36:16,341 --> 00:36:17,536
Okay.

610
00:36:31,022 --> 00:36:35,153
Look, Mario, I have a job
to do, so whatever this is...

611
00:36:35,360 --> 00:36:39,229
When you told Tetch to kill Lee,
you knew he would do the opposite.

612
00:36:40,065 --> 00:36:42,660
You sacrificed your
girlfriend for my fiancée.

613
00:36:42,834 --> 00:36:45,736
- That's insane.
- Can we just admit you still love her?

614
00:36:46,838 --> 00:36:48,238
- I don't have time for this.
- Hey!

615
00:36:49,674 --> 00:36:53,008
You once told me that if I
ever hurt her Lee, you'd kill me.

616
00:36:53,211 --> 00:36:55,146
Well, now it's my turn.

617
00:36:55,346 --> 00:36:59,215
I love Lee, and I'll do
whatever I have to to keep her.

618
00:36:59,584 --> 00:37:03,021
Then word of advice,
lose the jealousy.

619
00:37:04,456 --> 00:37:05,456
It's weak.

620
00:37:07,859 --> 00:37:09,157
Gordon.

621
00:37:13,164 --> 00:37:14,223
(SPITS)

622
00:37:18,903 --> 00:37:20,565
For Lee, I'll give you that one.

623
00:37:38,056 --> 00:37:39,888
Oh, Captain.

624
00:37:40,225 --> 00:37:41,465
If you keep frowning like that,

625
00:37:41,626 --> 00:37:43,746
you'll never get those
wrinkles out around your mouth.

626
00:37:45,730 --> 00:37:47,164
Come down to my office tomorrow.

627
00:37:48,466 --> 00:37:50,833
I'll give you a free evaluation.

628
00:37:55,573 --> 00:37:57,235
- (GRUNTING)
- (GROANING)

629
00:37:57,475 --> 00:38:00,741
I'm surprised you can feel that
through that thing you call a face.

630
00:38:00,945 --> 00:38:02,413
What are you doing? (GRUNTS)

631
00:38:02,647 --> 00:38:04,275
What I should
have done all along.

632
00:38:07,385 --> 00:38:08,614
(PANTING)

633
00:38:09,220 --> 00:38:10,711
You're insane.

634
00:38:11,456 --> 00:38:12,788
Oh, no, Doc.

635
00:38:13,091 --> 00:38:15,185
I'm saner than I've ever been.

636
00:38:15,693 --> 00:38:20,154
I'm seeing things clearly
for the very first time.

637
00:38:21,232 --> 00:38:23,531
All these years, I've put
my trust in the system,

638
00:38:23,768 --> 00:38:25,566
my trust in the law,

639
00:38:26,104 --> 00:38:28,835
held myself back from doing
what I really wanted to do.

640
00:38:31,676 --> 00:38:35,374
And then I saw the truth.
It's not just you that's guilty.

641
00:38:35,780 --> 00:38:37,874
- (BOTH GRUNTING)
- (CHOKING)

642
00:38:38,216 --> 00:38:39,912
This whole city is guilty.

643
00:38:40,151 --> 00:38:41,983
Stop. (CONTINUES CHOKING)

644
00:38:42,887 --> 00:38:45,550
You're a police
officer for God's sake.

645
00:38:46,524 --> 00:38:48,493
You have to follow the law.

646
00:38:48,760 --> 00:38:51,594
I don't have to do
anything. I am the law.

647
00:38:52,030 --> 00:38:53,555
I am judge,

648
00:38:55,166 --> 00:38:56,166
jury,

649
00:38:57,268 --> 00:38:59,294
and executioner!

650
00:39:00,839 --> 00:39:02,637
(SCREAMING)

651
00:39:03,775 --> 00:39:05,300
(HORN BLARING)

652
00:39:11,015 --> 00:39:12,677
Sentence served.

653
00:39:27,665 --> 00:39:28,792
Ed.

654
00:39:30,501 --> 00:39:33,369
- How'd she take it?
- What? Oh. Uh...

655
00:39:34,072 --> 00:39:36,803
Everything is wonderful.

656
00:39:37,942 --> 00:39:41,379
Isabella showed me that,
uh, I was worried over nothing.

657
00:39:49,454 --> 00:39:51,252
I'm so happy for you.

658
00:39:52,023 --> 00:39:53,616
But, why are you back?

659
00:39:53,825 --> 00:39:56,727
Well, she had to go to
her conference. I insisted.

660
00:39:57,095 --> 00:39:58,723
You're a good man.

661
00:39:59,464 --> 00:40:02,263
But, you look done in. I will
hear all about it tomorrow.

662
00:40:02,901 --> 00:40:04,426
Get some sleep.

663
00:40:17,148 --> 00:40:19,083
Got to give her credit.

664
00:40:19,450 --> 00:40:21,214
She fought for him.

665
00:40:22,120 --> 00:40:24,112
Too bad she
underestimated her opponent.

666
00:40:26,524 --> 00:40:29,119
- I'm assuming it's done.
- Yup.

667
00:40:29,394 --> 00:40:30,953
<i>Feel kind of bad though, boss.</i>

668
00:40:31,963 --> 00:40:33,625
I always liked librarians.

669
00:40:34,032 --> 00:40:35,091
You?

670
00:40:35,733 --> 00:40:37,463
What about poor Ed?

671
00:40:39,003 --> 00:40:40,904
He will be heartbroken.

672
00:40:42,607 --> 00:40:46,271
(SNIFFLES) Luckily, he
has a shoulder to cry on.

673
00:40:47,045 --> 00:40:48,343
(HUMMING)

674
00:40:52,917 --> 00:40:54,442
(BELL DINGING)

675
00:41:01,426 --> 00:41:03,418
Uh-oh. Come on. Oh, no.

676
00:41:05,730 --> 00:41:07,596
Oh, come on... Uh-oh.

677
00:41:09,167 --> 00:41:11,207
Come on, come on, come on,
come... (INHALES SHARPLY)

678
00:41:11,703 --> 00:41:13,501
Help me! Help me! Somebody help!

679
00:41:13,771 --> 00:41:14,771
Oh, dear!

680
00:41:15,006 --> 00:41:16,030
(CRASHING)

681
00:41:21,846 --> 00:41:24,008
Jim, you and Mario
have a heart-to-heart?

682
00:41:24,182 --> 00:41:25,548
Yeah. Where's Symon?

683
00:41:25,950 --> 00:41:28,283
No luck. He must've skedaddled.

684
00:41:29,787 --> 00:41:31,813
- I thought he might be at the bar.
- Uh-huh.

685
00:41:32,023 --> 00:41:34,151
Look, keep a perimeter
in case he shows back up.

686
00:41:34,459 --> 00:41:35,859
I'm gonna head to his house.

687
00:41:36,160 --> 00:41:38,925
And, Harvey, uh,
take it easy, huh?

688
00:41:39,097 --> 00:41:40,998
It's good to have
you back again, Jim.

689
00:41:41,165 --> 00:41:42,963
- Uh-huh.
- I'm real glad.

690
00:41:45,203 --> 00:41:46,432
Captain.

691
00:41:46,771 --> 00:41:48,433
- Did you hear?
- Everything.

692
00:41:48,706 --> 00:41:51,369
I saw Symon here earlier.
You managed to pick him up?

693
00:41:51,542 --> 00:41:54,637
Not yet. He must've skipped out
when we showed up. We'll get him.

694
00:41:55,046 --> 00:41:58,346
Alvarez said you were bringing in
the guy who did Paulie Pennies?

695
00:41:58,516 --> 00:42:00,246
Turned out to be a dead end.

696
00:42:01,386 --> 00:42:02,979
I'll let you know
when I find Symon.

697
00:42:03,154 --> 00:42:04,417
Jim.

698
00:42:05,189 --> 00:42:07,715
Things are gonna
change around here.

699
00:42:08,192 --> 00:42:10,192
<i>You and I are gonna make
a difference in this city.</i>

700
00:42:11,629 --> 00:42:13,530
We're gonna clean it up.

701
00:42:14,932 --> 00:42:16,195
Yes, sir.

702
00:42:30,648 --> 00:42:31,775
VOICES: <i>Guilty!</i>

703
00:42:32,150 --> 00:42:33,150
<i>Guilty.</i>

704
00:42:33,418 --> 00:42:34,545
<i>Guilty.</i>

705
00:42:34,786 --> 00:42:35,947
<i>- Guilty. Guilty.</i>
- (LAUGHING)

706
00:42:36,187 --> 00:42:37,382
<i>Guilty!</i>

707
00:42:38,623 --> 00:42:39,682
<i>Guilty!</i>

708
00:42:39,924 --> 00:42:41,153
<i>Guilty!</i>

709
00:42:41,859 --> 00:42:43,157
<i>Guilty.</i>

710
00:42:43,394 --> 00:42:45,363
<i>Guilty. Guilty.</i>

711
00:42:46,130 --> 00:42:48,031
<i>Guilty.</i>

712
00:42:48,766 --> 00:42:49,961
(WOMAN SCREAMS)

713
00:42:53,771 --> 00:42:55,364
GCPD. Sir!

714
00:42:56,140 --> 00:42:57,631
(GROANING)

715
00:43:01,579 --> 00:43:02,911
Dr. Symon.

716
00:43:05,650 --> 00:43:07,016
Who did this?

717
00:43:11,823 --> 00:43:13,291
Barnes.

718
00:43:27,505 --> 00:43:29,497
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

719
00:44:02,540 --> 00:44:03,540
English -SDH
